For the St. Johns River...including Above Lake Harney...Moderate\nflooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Above Lake Harney.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Water enters the first story of homes on\nWhitcomb Drive between Crossover Lane and Lake Harney Road. Water\ncovers Mullet Lake Park.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 AM EST Saturday the stage was 9.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 6.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 AM EST Saturday was 9.1 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 9.0 feet.\n- Flood stage is 8.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Sunday morning at 1130 AM EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 141444"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0007.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.baf82163ebc7a13c2c2973bb2b498e5f5e98330d.001.1,2026-11-12T20:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2305617cfc87570d35c0272f7b095ee20824c465.001.1,2026-11-12T08:23:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.74c745e794d1d8e559a07c71e20e072593439e0f.001.1,2026-11-11T20:45:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1090a929c84ca5c60e1fa1e2c1f9abd629f2547d.001.1,2026-11-11T08:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4cb99847a805aeb5278526ed5fadc4317dba317.001.1,2026-11-10T19:49:00-05:00 w-n