low-water crossings along the Gila River.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSPSR"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS85 KPSR 140224"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING FOR THE UPSTREAM RELEASE OF PAINTED ROCK DAM ON THE GILA RIVER REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 AM MST TUESDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KPSR.FA.W.0044.000000T0000Z-261117T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-17T11:00:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bec63c30ca2aef1914061195bebb9a26e519d8bd.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.5,29.08],[-81.69,29.32],[-81.57,29.35],[-81.42,29.1],[-81.5,29.08]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bec63c30ca2aef1914061195bebb9a26e519d8bd.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bec63c30ca2aef1914061195bebb9a26e519d8bd.001.1","areaDesc":"Lake, FL; Volusia, FL","geocode":{"SAME":["012069","012127"],"UGC":["FLC069","FLC127"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC069","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC127"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c257a163ba9a34435b3a2682162c0d586ebd35d1.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c257a163ba9a34435b3a2682162c0d586ebd35d1.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-13T10:18:00-05:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.857595aa2a45e296dce61da83545908cf13c839f.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.857595aa2a45e296dce61da83545908cf13c839f.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-14T09:40:00-05:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.186f04232826ecc706470a21f19efb20ca82f35f.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.186f04232826ecc706470a21f19efb20ca82f35f.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-13T20:21:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-11-14T10:14:00-05:00","effective":"2026-11-14T10:14:00-05:00","onset":"2026-11-14T10:14:00-05:00","expires":"2026-11-15T11:30:00-05:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 14 at 10:14AM EST by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Volusia and Lake Counties.\n\n.On the St Johns River at Astor, slight rises within Minor Flood\nStage are forecast this weekend into next week due to a combination\nof northerly winds, downstream tidal effects, and water from upstream\nheavy rainfall working north through the basin.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 3.5 feet, Canals have overflowed into yards. Homes on\nor near Wildhog, Bonnet and Snail roads become inaccessible with\nseveral inches of water inside homes along the river and canals.\nDocks at Astor Bridge marina and throughout Astor are completely\nsubmerged. Bartram Rd and Holiday Circle are inaccessible with\nyards completely submerged. Clair Street is inaccessible. Roads\nflooded in South Moon Fish Camp, docks and yards at condominiums on\nJuno Trail and water breaches the sea wall at Blair's Jungle Den.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:30 AM EST Saturday the stage was 2.6 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 9:30 AM EST Saturday was 2.7 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to 3.4 feet just after\nmidnight tonight. Additional rises are possible thereafter.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Sunday morning at 1130 AM EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 141514"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0003.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4ef59d32457f355844009fc6a804489f4a4901b9.001.1,2026-11-12T20:58:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c0218479c9cb47f9409b0644c9e2600ae039c28c.001.1,2026-11-12T08:06:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.77e928eff45837bf21c2096869d876897004b858.001.1,2026-11-11T20:34:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.565ab76ad642c089ac96855029c39f195a976025.001.1,2026-11-11T08:46:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.505e8f7bcdba7736f6bbdd92a1fa13719b15a01e.001.1,2026-11-10T19:47:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e107256a42b0530b65688e8f07bafebc7c640d16.001.1,2026-11-10T09:29:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9cf3f462f33a5e4d6ad2b4caef1b80879d8052b.001.1,2026-11-09T09:16:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4b285fc635ac6e22d5ca2389fc92c65dc81f18f7.001.1,2026-11-09T20:01:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9d2563c5250d1a21cbb48